== Successor ==
The successor of the Agera called the [[Koenigsegg Jesko|Jesko]] was unveiled at the 2019 Geneva Motor Show. The potential replacement was shown to prospective buyers via VR in an event held in Australia by the company beforehand.<ref>{{cite web |title=These are the last ever Koenigsegg Agera RS hypercars |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/these-are-last-ever-koenigsegg-agera-rs-hypercars |website=TopGear.com |date=9 July 2018 |access-date=13 September 2018 |archive-date=14 September 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180914022444/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/these-are-last-ever-koenigsegg-agera-rs-hypercars |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="Top Gear"/>

